+# ADR-0017: Journey publishes `journey.task-completed`; identity records the welcome call
+
+- **Status:** Proposed
+- **Date:** 2026-11-16
+- **Deciders:** <second person to approve>
+- **Sources:** A4-C-005 (task events in the event catalogue), T3-O-005, [event conventions](../conventions/events.md), [draft spec](../specs/draft-welcome-call/spec.md)
+
+## Context
+
+Head office wants to see which persons have had their welcome call. The call is a task of kind `welcome-call` in the `journey` module; the person record is owned by `identity`. When the task is completed, the person record must change. A module never calls another module to write (hard rule 3), so the change needs an event. The event catalogue already plans task events (A4-C-005). No event leaves `journey` today.
+
+## Options
+
+1. **Generic `journey.task-completed` with the task kind.** Identity subscribes and acts on kind `welcome-call`. Good: one event for every later reaction to a completed task (bonuses A1-C-024, the 72-hour rule A4-C-004). Bad: identity knows one task kind name.
+2. **Specific `journey.welcome-call-completed`.** Good: identity does not know task kinds. Bad: one event per kind with a reaction; journey must know which kinds others care about.
+3. **Identity reads the tasks through the journey API when head office asks.** Good: no new column. Bad: head office's view becomes a cross-module query; `getPerson` cannot return the value on its own.
+
+## Decision
+
+We choose option 1. A completed task is a fact of `journey`; which completions matter is the decision of the reacting module. The payload is `taskId`, `personId`, `kind`, `completedAt` (IDs and a time, no personal data copied). `occurredAt` equals `completedAt`. A task is completed once; completing it again returns the task and publishes nothing.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Other modules can react to completed tasks without a change to `journey`.
+- Identity holds the constant `WELCOME_CALL_KIND = "welcome-call"`. A rename of the kind must change both; the test in `apps/worker/src/worker.test.ts` covers the path.
+- The handler is idempotent: a redelivered event sets the same `welcomedAt`.
+- `pnpm docs` checks the Events tables of both module files against the code; `pnpm arch` keeps the dependency one-way (identity → journey types only).
