@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# draft-welcome-call: Record on the person when the welcome call is done
+
+- **Jira:** none yet (direct request). A person creates the story and renames this folder to `AN-<n>`
+- **Gate:** design (trigger 2: new event `journey.task-completed`)
+- **Status:** Draft
+- **Approved-by:**
+- **Baseline:** Discovery v0.1
+- **Module:** journey. Touches: identity (consumes `journey.task-completed`), apps/worker (wiring)
+
+## Context
+
+Head office wants to see which persons have had their welcome call. The call is a `journey` task of kind `welcome-call`; the person record is in `identity`. Decision: [ADR-0017](../../adr/0017-journey-task-completed-event.md).
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+No Discovery AC covers this request. The tests are named by behaviour, without an AC ID.
+
+| Behaviour | Test |
+|---|---|
+| `completeTask` sets `completedAt`, returns the task, publishes the event; fails for an unknown task | `packages/core/src/journey/journey.test.ts` |
+| `welcomedAt` is `null` at first; `getPerson` returns it; only kind `welcome-call` sets it | `packages/core/src/identity/identity.test.ts` |
+| `app.journey.completeTask` sets `welcomedAt` across modules | `apps/worker/src/worker.test.ts` |
+
+## Design increment
+
+- **Module file `journey`:** `.completeTask(taskId)`, `TaskNotFoundError`, `TaskCompleted`; emits `journey.task-completed`; invariant: a task is completed once.
+- **Module file `identity`:** `registerIdentitySubscriptions(bus, { repo })`, `WELCOME_CALL_KIND`, `IdentitySubscriptionDeps`; `Person.welcomedAt`; consumes `journey.task-completed`; invariant on `welcomedAt`.
+- **Contracts:** `journey.task-completed`, payload `taskId`, `personId`, `kind`, `completedAt` (ISO). `occurredAt` = `completedAt`.
+- **Schema:**
+  - `journey.task.completed_at`: timestamptz, nullable. Not personal (task data, kept under T3-O-005).
+  - `identity.person.welcomed_at`: timestamptz, nullable. Personal: category `other`, purpose "Show head office which persons have had their welcome call", owner `identity`, retention `account lifetime + 3 years`.
+
+## Local decisions
+
+- Completing a completed task returns it unchanged and publishes nothing: the completion time stays the first one.
+- `TaskRepository` and `PersonRepository` get `update` (and `findById` for tasks): needed to change a stored record.
+- A `journey.task-completed` event for an unknown person is ignored: the person may be deleted (data-subject request).
+- `welcomedAt` shows the latest welcome call of the person. An event with an earlier `completedAt` (a redelivery out of order) does not move it back.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- The head office portal screen that lists the persons.
+- Reopening a task; a production Drizzle repository and its migration.
+
+## Open questions
+
+- Retention of `welcomed_at`: the data protection officer sets it (T3-O-005). The draft uses the account default `account lifetime + 3 years`; confirm or change at approval.
+- Category of `welcomed_at`: `other` (a fact of the customer relationship). Confirm at approval.
+
+## Deviations
+
+None.
